048582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124752 #edb/ref 1050 780.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124752 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "9faeb18a-39f2-528b-927a-5e59d0f90fc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125253 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125253 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97587" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125253 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125253 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125253 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e241e927-1969-5b14-8d05-12ee0adb39d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125253 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125440 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125440 #edb/ref 1061 20152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125440 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9ee24e02-1f78-5b25-8d1c-f19b4a0052ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125440 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125441 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125441 #edb/ref 1061 20154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125441 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d4cf88b7-d61d-5b12-a8f6-f786898cb8c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125441 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125442 #edb/ref 1061 20155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125442 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "80774b4b-be41-5637-b9a9-f728e8911827" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125442 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125546 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125546 #edb/ref 1061 31941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125546 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a48f8724-cd55-576f-8431-f47c3d90338a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125546 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125547 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125547 #edb/ref 1061 31942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125547 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f3a9b6e8-c0c7-5e91-a3fa-8081e91b886a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125547 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125548 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125548 #edb/ref 1061 31944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125548 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "14e61c95-f43b-5c3d-8e38-75c4db0838d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125548 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125799 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's suppose we have the linear map\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T: {\\color{blue}V} \\to {\\color{red}W}\n$$\n\nwhere the bases of the vector spaces $\\color{blue}V$ and ${\\color{red}W}$ respectively are given by\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}}=\\{ {\\color{blue}\\mathbf{b}_1},{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{b}_2}, {\\color{blue}\\mathbf{b}_3} \\}, \\qquad \\qquad {\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}} = \\{ {\\color{red}\\mathbf{c}_1},{\\color{red}\\mathbf{c}_2} \\}.\n$$\n\nThe **matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ with respect to the bases $\\color{blue}\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}$** is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}({\\color{blue}\\mathbf{b}_1}),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\color{blue}{\\mathbf{b}_2}),$ and $\\mathbf{T}({\\color{blue}\\mathbf{b}_3})$ relative to the basis ${\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B|C} & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ [T({b}_{1})]_{C} & [T({b}_{2})]_{C} & [T({b}_{3})]_{C} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, if \n\n![](images/be/be8cff88ef83ebc67d0df7a50a243c55c8f11aa92e7a07f64b73bb30ed701392.svg)\n\nthen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B|C} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 10 & -12 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125799 #edb/ref 1065 3589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125799 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "da91373e-0973-56a4-91c9-aa2a2b1de0b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125799 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125843 #edb/ref 1064 "Given the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of a linear map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\to W$ relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C},$ and the coordinates $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ of a vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to $\\mathcal{B},$ the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ with respect to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ can be found as \n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}} = \n[\\mathbf{T}]_{{\\mathcal{B}}|{\\mathcal{C}}}\\cdot [\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}\n$$\n\nFor example, if\n\n![](images/e3/e3623ffb88602004ad3ab01f55976d3a55759563a6088f4e2a10b7b8849a6f70.svg)\n\nthen the image of $\\mathbf x$ under $\\mathbf T$ relative to $\\mathcal C$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125843 #edb/ref 1065 5093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125843 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "db73b6f4-55d4-5d30-856e-463bc6cc9964" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125843 #edb/ref 1067 "The Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given by a Matrix Relative to Two Bases" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269657 #edb/ref 1080 "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269657 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269657 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b3d3be8-279d-59f3-a2d8-12ca9d0cce23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270458 #edb/ref 1080 "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270458 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270458 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "89a50b23-711d-5633-b7dd-e7d9b60ebde7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270790 #edb/ref 1080 "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270790 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270790 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa59da11-d54d-5e37-89f9-271bc5567df8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270920 #edb/ref 1080